{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti","id":1074886,"title":"Controlling Paradox (Scelesti)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-07T15:48:52-07:00","id":1074886,"title":"Controlling Paradox (Scelesti)","content":"So, being new to the 2nd edition of Mage, explain this to me like I'm five: how do Mages invite Paradox into their spells, thus corrupting them and making them more powerful? How is this addicting? Provided examples would be awesome.<br /> <br /> Secondly, how does swearing yourself to an Abyssal Watchtower or gaining a Scelesti Legacy work in this new edition? What benefits does it grant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There was a signature here. It's gone now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8730-pandorym","name":"Pandorym","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8730_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T16:26:51-07:00","id":1074899,"title":"","content":"The 2e version of the least degree of Abyssal initiation works kind of like anti-containment of Paradox; you release the Paradox and roll Gnosis, and each success lets you control how one Paradox Reach gets applied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T16:37:03-07:00","id":1074902,"title":"","content":"Swearing yourself to an Abyssal Watchtower or joining/creating an Abyssal Legacy has not yet gotten any rules in 2E. As of now we only got the core book and a few entries in Dark Eras and Dark Eras Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T22:38:51-07:00","id":1075011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1074902#post1074902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swearing yourself to an Abyssal Watchtower or joining/creating an Abyssal Legacy has not yet gotten any rules in 2E. As of now we only got the core book and a few entries in Dark Eras and Dark Eras Companion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where abouts in the book are these references, Tessie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T23:21:30-07:00","id":1075020,"title":"","content":"238-239 with the system rules being the start of 239 for inviting paradox. I lack the dark age parts if that's what you're asking. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T23:23:29-07:00","id":1075022,"title":"","content":"Swearing to an Abyssal Watchtower could also give you the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/603390-homebrew-abyssal-arcanum\"><b>Abyssal Arcanum.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T03:05:18-07:00","id":1075056,"title":"","content":"That's homebrew.<br /> <br /> We haven't had time yet to 2e the Scelesti mechanics beyond the one-line description of first initiation everyone's talking about. You can, if you know how to, attempt to control how a Paradox manifests, but the process is extremely addictive and runs the risk of you becoming a second-stage Scelesti (a Nasnasi), where your Path symbols are corrupted by their abyssal antitheses, your ability to summon supernal creatures is replaced by one to summon Gulmoth, and your nimbus is poisioned.<br /> <br /> Third initiation Scelesti are just those with Legacies, some of which require you to be a Nasnas. <br /> <br /> Fourth Initiation Scelesti are those who bargain with the Aeon of Paradox for the ability to mess with the Paradox roll, not just how any Paradox appears. Their powers require the most work.<br /> <br /> The thing that we're noodling about, playtesting when Scelesti come up in our games, is to replace Wisdom for Nasnasi-and-up Scelesti to represent their fucked-up natures. Scelesti probably become Qliphoth instead of Mad Ones when they completely go off the edge.<br /> <br /> Oh, right, yeah. A Qliphoth is a mage who is a walking Iris to a Annunaki, spawning Gulmoth wherever they go. They're in the &quot;way too powerful for even most mages to do anything other than run&quot; category along with Exarchal avatars and archmasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T04:17:36-07:00","id":1075068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075056#post1075056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that we're noodling about, playtesting when Scelesti come up in our games, is to replace Wisdom for Nasnasi-and-up Scelesti to represent their fucked-up natures. Scelesti probably become Qliphoth instead of Mad Ones when they completely go off the edge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... sounds amazing. I have to wonder what you guys might think would be an appropriate replacement for Wisdom. My first thoughts might run towards themes like &quot;Control&quot; if I think of a Qliphoth as their 0-integrity result - or for a warped take on Wisdom, &quot;Restraint&quot;. I am legitimately curious what the opposite end of a Qliphoth might look like in your vision. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T04:51:24-07:00","id":1075077,"title":"","content":"Lemee chck my Developer folder notes...<br /> <br /> Yeah, so my version currently calls it &quot;Joining&quot; after the original name for the second initiation from back in Tome of Mysteries; it goes up where Wisdom goes down. 0 Joining you turn back into a normal Mage with Wisdom 1 (it was always canonical that nasnasi could, in theory, go cold turkey and return to normalcy), 10 Joining turns you into a Qliphoth, the trick to being a Scelestus is to fuck your Path's symbolism just enough but not too much; to draw on your linked Annunaki without being consumed by it. The experiments are in what causes it to go up and down; what's a &quot;sin&quot; for a Scelestus?<br /> <br /> It's a parallel to Tremere, who in the protoype 2e notes replace their Gnosis with &quot;Hollow&quot;, the trait that lets their Gnosis consume the soul currently attached to it as fuel, gives them Houses instead of Legacies, and so on. The Tremere are the most complex fallen mages because they're both an altered template , a group of not-exactly-Legacies and an Order, and it's figuring out what parts of them are inherent powers, what's the various Legacies they've consumed being turned into Houses, and what's the Tremere-Order-Status-only Merit equivalents to Egregore, etc that's the trick. But Tremere *do* use Wisdom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T04:56:37-07:00","id":1075081,"title":"","content":"I should note that I intended to get the Scelsti, Mad One, and Tremere rules out by now, but paying work must come first. However, Deviant has mechanical things to say about &quot;altered templates&quot; that are coming in handy when thinking about them, so it's not wasted time. That my time's eaten by preparing a game that's required time and attention on a parallel topic is a lucky coincidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T05:20:20-07:00","id":1075084,"title":"","content":"I'm so confused when reading these Scelesti terms. I vaguely remember them from Left Hand Path, but I don't own it. Should I murder...erm, borrow it from my friend when the Dark Trio Rules come out, or will I be able to understand and use them just with the corebook? <br /> This probably doubles as a question from my GM, because if so, she will want to make notes from the LHP to in order to quench her anxiety.<br /> Tremere stuff makes me more excited about it each time I read it, so good job with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T05:54:26-07:00","id":1075092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075077#post1075077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lemee chck my Developer folder notes...<br /> <br /> Yeah, so my version currently calls it &quot;Joining&quot; after the original name for the second initiation from back in Tome of Mysteries; it goes up where Wisdom goes down. 0 Joining you turn back into a normal Mage with Wisdom 1 (it was always canonical that nasnasi could, in theory, go cold turkey and return to normalcy), 10 Joining turns you into a Qliphoth, the trick to being a Scelestus is to fuck your Path's symbolism just enough but not too much; to draw on your linked Annunaki without being consumed by it. The experiments are in what causes it to go up and down; what's a &quot;sin&quot; for a Scelestus?</div> </div> </div> </div>The concept behind that is even better than I originally thought it would be. I look forward to seeing the full thing when you finish <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T05:59:21-07:00","id":1075093,"title":"","content":"Sure. So, a brief lexicon of the Scelesti<br /> <br /> Scelestus - a mage convicted of dealing with the Abyss. The Pentacle recognises four main classifications (&quot;initiations&quot;) of Scelsti, in order of severity.<br /> <br /> Rabashakim - first initiation Scelesti, guilty of casting Befouled spells. The only form of being a Scelestus that doesn't carry a death penalty in most gold laws, though some Consilia will kill you for it anyway.<br /> <br /> Befouled spell - a spell where, mechanically, you then roll Gnosis to direct how any Paradox reach is spent. Rabashakim can only cast Befouled praxes or rotes, and they can't make the rotes. Each Befouled spell cast worsens the addiction to the practice, which if unchecked can lead to the mage becoming a Nasnasi<br /> <br /> Antominian spell - another term for a Befouled spell<br /> <br /> Nasnasi - second initiation Scelesti, whose Path has become corrupted by a Dur Abzu, inverting their Path symbols, turning their natural Summoning Gulmoth-wards and doing weird things to their Wisdom. Can cast Befouled improvised spells and write Befouled rotes. Technically rehabilitatable, but most Consilia won't bother, they'll just kill captured Nasnasi out of hand.<br /> <br /> Dur Abzu - the abyssal &quot;Paths&quot;, centered on antisymbols the Nasnasi call Ziggurats instead of Watchtowers.<br /> <br /> Shedim / Autarch - third-initiation Scelesti, guilty of organizing and recruiting others of their kind. Beyond the point where good intentions and addiction can excuse the Scelestus' behaviour. Technically speaking, a Shedim has created a Scelestus Nameless Order while an Autarch has created a Scelestus Legacy, but it gets confusing and the Pentacle often treat them interchangeably.<br /> <br /> Baalim - A Scelestus who has achieved control over Paradox itself, being able to shape and direct it. Usually gained by bargaining with the Other. The highest crime on the Pentacle's books.<br /> <br /> Elder Diadem - the abilities of a Baalim<br /> <br /> Acamoth - an abyssal entity formed from corruption in the astral realms<br /> <br /> Gulmoth - an abyssal entity formed from corruption in the physical and adjacent worlds<br /> <br /> Annunaki - an abyssal world/being<br /> <br /> Qliphoth - a mage who has become hollowed-out into a walking gateway to an Annunaki<br /> <br /> The Other / the Old Man - the Aeon (rank 7 Goetia) that represents Paradox in the Anima Mundi, and acts almost like the Annunaki's &quot;ambassador&quot; to the Fallen World. Bears a striking physical resemblence to Voormas, the metaplot villain of Mage: The Ascension.<br /> <br /> Aswadim - archmasters who promote the Abyss as part of their intended direction for the Fallen World. Stand apart from the heirarchy in that they usually weren't Scelesti before becoming archmasters, and use the others as pawns. Meet using the Other's astral domain as neutral ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T06:18:43-07:00","id":1075097,"title":"","content":"In any case, the wordcount pressures and priorities for the corebook were such that we made the hard call - we couldmonly provide playable rules for one of the Pentacle's enemies, and in service to The Fallen World Chronicle (and efficiency, as they have the least special rules) we went for the Seers. If you're a storyteller, you don't *need* any of the rules for Joining we're working on - just to know that a Nasnasi can roll Gnosis and control how Paradox Reach is spent on released paradoxes. I guess the full rules with conditions for creating a Befouled Praxis or learning a Befouled rote (and therefore being a rabashakim) will be interesting for troupes wanting their pcs to play with fire, but part of me does wonder how many people would actually <i>use</i> systems for being a Baal.<br /> <br /> Tremere, though, are an Order. A secretive, hated-by-the-others Order who were expelled from the Diamond in the middle ages for eating souls, but they're the point where the venn diagram bubbles of &quot;Nameless Order&quot;, &quot;Legacy,&quot; &quot;Reaper&quot; and &quot;Lich&quot; all meet. If they were Abyssal, too, they'd be all the Mage bad guys combined!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T06:22:34-07:00","id":1075098,"title":"","content":"Thanks! While I usually prefer plain English for stuff, dark magics are a special case as them being mysterious and preferably from a obscure dead language is kind of the part of the charm. This is super useful and should invite discomfort just from hearing these terms at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T06:51:59-07:00","id":1075103,"title":"","content":"I like the commentary on the usual reactions of Consilia. It's a nice reminder of how other Awakened actually see this stuff.<br /> <br /> It makes me wonder how hostile the Abyss usually is. I always got the sensation that the Abyss is antithetical and inimical to all sane existence, and thus erodes the world around it like lye on skin; that Abyssal creatures are nightmares that revel in pain and destruction. Yet that doesn't quite seem to fit the full length of the anti-reality that the Abyss represents, especially given that one of the example Aswad's grand plans is to create a &quot;peaceful&quot; world by pulling it out of the Abyss. It feels like bartering with inherently intensely and directly destructive deities would be suicidal, at best.<br /> <br /> And yet Scelesti do it and get away with it. One can only help but wonder how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:01:15-07:00","id":1075106,"title":"","content":"I always kinda assumed that the dangerous nightmarish pain seeking soul ripping Abyssal creatures are the most common (or rather, the most visible), because they are the ones to actually come after you on their own, while most of the just-nightmarish and just-wrong things tend to...not be so visible. Or at least, don't make such noise in the community.<br /> Though even the well-intended Abyssal creature will cause destruction, not due to being malignous, but simply because the way they do things is probably misaligned with reality and will clash with it on the principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:22:54-07:00","id":1075111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It feels like bartering with inherently intensely and directly destructive deities would be suicidal, at best. </div> </div> </div>Suicide is a common end for Scelesti.<br /> <br /> The Aswadim are an exception I'd guess because Archmasters are an exception. It's noticable that Samiel isn't really a Scelesti ideologically, he just wants something and from the point of view of a posthuman god, the Abyss is just a tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:31:55-07:00","id":1075118,"title":"","content":"Well, where the Tremere (sorry to keep on at this comparison) are an Order with their own legends, foundational beliefs, etc, most of the above is <i>imposed</i> on the Scelesti instead of being owned by them. A Baal won't call himself that, but a Consilium that captures and tries him will. The Diamond's reaction to mages who willingly harness (or try to, anyway) the antithetical nature of the Abyss and reject Meaning is to damn well stamp Meaning all over them, and put them in a linguistic box marked &quot;Nasnasi&quot; or whathaveyou.<br /> <br /> The Abyss contains everything and nothing. Theoretically, some things in it could be &quot;better&quot; than what's real, but they always come with a generous side serving of Zalgo. That Aswad in Imperial Mysteries is, remember, trying to very carefully isolate one single abyssal symbol and then use his archmastery to make it all work out okay. Less advanced dabblers in the ways of the Annunaki don't have the tools Imperial Arcana give you.<br /> <br /> For example, I could easily see a foolish mage attempting to find someone who'd died (or at least, a version of them where they hadn't) in the Abyss, because anything Not Real is in there, and getting a human-shaped thing from the Prince of 10,000 Leaves that resembles their goal. they keep the thing locked up safely, but eventually notice that all children born within a mile of it have carnivorous fangs or something.<br /> <br /> Gulmoth aren't evil spirits. They're coding errors in reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:41:35-07:00","id":1075124,"title":"","content":"Reactions also vary by Order - a Silver Ladder mage who casts a Befouled rote once to achieve a set goal and never touches it again is a badass if he gets caught, a Guardian of the Veil who does it will be lucky to walk away with intact frontal lobes.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason the Orders dress Befouling up in Babylonian terminology and make Rabashakim out to be different, somehow, is that they don't want neophyte mages knowing how <i>easy</i> it is.<br /> <br /> But just as abstinance is the worst sex education policy, making abyssal magic more Mysterious than it is just means those who find put about it and experiment with it do so without a safety net AND go hardcore quicker. you get way fewer Rabashakim, but more of them blow up into Nasnasi.<br /> <br /> Again with the Tremere side-commentary, but the major fallout of the Tremere's banishment is that well-meaning Legacies who have extreme longevity or immortality among their practices have to hush it up in polite company, and the modern Pentacle knows way less about Souls and how they work than their ancestors from a few thousand years ago, because Souls were the Tremere's &quot;thing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T07:47:03-07:00","id":1075127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075118#post1075118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, I could easily see a foolish mage attempting to find someone who'd died (or at least, a version of them where they hadn't) in the Abyss, because anything Not Real is in there, and getting a human-shaped thing from the Prince of 10,000 Leaves that resembles their goal. they keep the thing locked up safely, but eventually notice that all children born within a mile of it have carnivorous fangs or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been my go-to example for why someone would dabble with the Abyss for years, and was actually a major temptation offered to a Scelestus player character at one point; a chance at a universe where things <i>weren't</i> always chocked full of awful shit, and where he was actually a decent and functional human being.<br /> <br /> Went about as well as you'd expect.<br /> <br /> This is all good stuff, Dave. I look forward to seeing it if/when this ever makes it into books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T09:29:40-07:00","id":1075152,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always liked the &quot;place where non existant things are&quot;. Wanted to use that as a horror fodder for my Time Mages that collapsed timelines with Shifting Sands and pretended that everything that happened there had no bearing because it never happened.<br /> &quot;Hi, I'm your victim from a timeline that you erased, and I'm animated by Abyss exactly because of that&quot; always gave me chills. That and &quot;HIM IM THE DAUGHTER YOU COULD HAVE IF YOU FOLLOWED UP ON THE HIGHSCHOOL CRUSH&quot; and other things like these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T14:24:33-07:00","id":1075244,"title":"","content":"I always try to make Scelesti-the ones who aren't purely horror monsters, anyway-come off as polite and soft-spoken. Serene. Apostles of the Void.<br /> <br /> This is because of the fundamental temptation of the Abyss: <i>We can give you whatever you want. And we are fair in our asking prices. Desire is the only law here.</i><br /> <br /> The thing about the Abyss is, as Dave mentioned, it is not evil; it's an infection. A virus isn't killing you because it hates you, it's simply because hijacking your cells and commandeering your body to leap to other hosts is the only way it can survive and reproduce. Scelesti who accept that moniker tend to calmly explain that just as a body grows stronger from a vaccine, so are they helping people by infecting the world with impossibility; is that not what mages do all the time? Are they not the purest mages? <br /> <br /> Of course, the Abyss is not a virus, it's a reality. It's several realities, and all of them are different from our own in that they are all <i>broken.</i> And none of them can be fixed; the moment they are. they would cease being part of the Abyss, because something that makes sense is True, and the Abyss is a Lie.<br /> <br /> Naturally, very advanced Scelesti and Aswadim, upon having this pointed out, tend to smile softly. You're almost there! Just a little more! Now-ask yourself why the reward for their goals is the chance to hang up the non-euclidean sculpture and return to being normal mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T15:10:56-07:00","id":1075264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075077#post1075077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lemee chck my Developer folder notes...<br /> <br /> Yeah, so my version currently calls it &quot;Joining&quot; after the original name for the second initiation from back in Tome of Mysteries; it goes up where Wisdom goes down. 0 Joining you turn back into a normal Mage with Wisdom 1 (it was always canonical that nasnasi could, in theory, go cold turkey and return to normalcy), 10 Joining turns you into a Qliphoth, the trick to being a Scelestus is to fuck your Path's symbolism just enough but not too much; to draw on your linked Annunaki without being consumed by it. The experiments are in what causes it to go up and down; what's a &quot;sin&quot; for a Scelestus?<br /> <br /> It's a parallel to Tremere, who in the protoype 2e notes replace their Gnosis with &quot;Hollow&quot;, the trait that lets their Gnosis consume the soul currently attached to it as fuel, gives them Houses instead of Legacies, and so on. The Tremere are the most complex fallen mages because they're both an altered template , a group of not-exactly-Legacies and an Order, and it's figuring out what parts of them are inherent powers, what's the various Legacies they've consumed being turned into Houses, and what's the Tremere-Order-Status-only Merit equivalents to Egregore, etc that's the trick. But Tremere *do* use Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This all sounds so exciting!<br /> <br /> Was Joining something that goes up or down using XP or an Obsession, like Wisdom, or was it something that purely goes up and down from sins, like a Werewolf's Harmony?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T17:15:01-07:00","id":1075640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075077#post1075077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lemee chck my Developer folder notes...<br /> <br /> Yeah, so my version currently calls it &amp;quot;Joining&amp;quot; after the original name for the second initiation from back in Tome of Mysteries; it goes up where Wisdom goes down. 0 Joining you turn back into a normal Mage with Wisdom 1 (it was always canonical that nasnasi could, in theory, go cold turkey and return to normalcy), 10 Joining turns you into a Qliphoth, the trick to being a Scelestus is to fuck your Path's symbolism just enough but not too much; to draw on your linked Annunaki without being consumed by it. The experiments are in what causes it to go up and down; what's a &amp;quot;sin&amp;quot; for a Scelestus?<br /> <br /> It's a parallel to Tremere, who in the protoype 2e notes replace their Gnosis with &amp;quot;Hollow&amp;quot;, the trait that lets their Gnosis consume the soul currently attached to it as fuel, gives them Houses instead of Legacies, and so on. The Tremere are the most complex fallen mages because they're both an altered template , a group of not-exactly-Legacies and an Order, and it's figuring out what parts of them are inherent powers, what's the various Legacies they've consumed being turned into Houses, and what's the Tremere-Order-Status-only Merit equivalents to Egregore, etc that's the trick. But Tremere *do* use Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds AMAZING.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:34:49-07:00","id":1075996,"title":"","content":"So, let me get this straight: if a Mage invites Paradox into their improvised spell or Rote or what have you, they must choose to release the Paradox, not contain it. Then they roll Gnosis - for every success, they can control one Paradox Reach. But this is dangerous, because the practice is addicting due to the rush of power and exposure to the Abyss. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> A Mage who does this too much may be then tempted to learn Befouled (or antominian) Rotes and Praxes. Which I assume automatically overdraw on Reach and risk Paradox which must be controlled, but are more powerful than standard. Am I close?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There was a signature here. It's gone now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8730-pandorym","name":"Pandorym","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8730_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:15:42-07:00","id":1076105,"title":"","content":"That seems about the sum of it, yeah. In 1e, the addicting rush manifested as regaining a point of Willpower each time you cast an antinomian spell but then having to roll Resolve + Comp (with a cumulative -1 for each roll you resisted successfully past the first) for every spell you cast thereafter for an entire week. If you ever hit so high a penalty that you had a chance die, you risked becoming a Nasnasi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:26:51-07:00","id":1076196,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> said. And it was really cool! It was also really cumbersome cuz it was hard to memorize. The setbacks were stuff you could easily control for if you used the magic at say, a point in the chronicle that you knew a time-skip was coming up... :3<br /> <br /> But antinomian magic made it so that you were tempted to keep casting your next spells as antinomian, and everything else started becoming harder for the next half-a-day as you were constantly distracted by forms of abyssal confusion and hallucinations, like weird smells or itching. Basically all the drug tilts made-creepy., like axel said.<br /> <br /> But my favorite set-back... was the fact that any wounds you took would become <i>infected</i> by the abyss and were treated as Resistant, like when you try to contain a paradox. So if your spell was for self-defense and it wasn't enough to keep you from at least being injured, then you definitely paid the piper then!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T00:53:56-07:00","id":1076358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076196#post1076196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> said. And it was really cool! It was also really cumbersome cuz it was hard to memorize. The setbacks were stuff you could easily control for if you used the magic at say, a point in the chronicle that you knew a time-skip was coming up... :3<br /> <br /> But antinomian magic made it so that you were tempted to keep casting your next spells as antinomian, and everything else started becoming harder for the next half-a-day as you were constantly distracted by forms of abyssal confusion and hallucinations, like weird smells or itching. Basically all the drug tilts made-creepy., like axel said.<br /> <br /> But my favorite set-back... was the fact that any wounds you took would become <i>infected</i> by the abyss and were treated as Resistant, like when you try to contain a paradox. So if your spell was for self-defense and it wasn't enough to keep you from at least being injured, then you definitely paid the piper then!</div> </div> </div> </div>All of this for one controlled Reach at Gnosis 3? What player would even consider this powerful or useful?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:14:08-07:00","id":1076366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076358#post1076358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of this for one controlled Reach at Gnosis 3? What player would even consider this powerful or useful?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! I've been wondering about that too. The 1E version just had all the effects happen wholesale, but I was thinking that the set-backs from the 1E antinomian magic would be like incentives to gain a bonus to your gnosis roll or something for additional controlled reach, or to even create additional successes on the paradox roll for even crazier high-risk high-reward gambles.<br /> <br /> For example, the 1e version has one of the effects being that you can spend mana to turn a forces 3 attack into goddamn aggravated damage! What if in 2E homebrew, you used a paradox reach to gain that effect instead. Meanwhile, you could use the infected-wounds penalty as a potential incentive, and if you agree to take that Condition, you increase the paradox successes by 1 but also gain +2 to your gnosis roll for taking control of the paradox, giving you a slight chance at gaining 1 more controlled-paradox-reach, but if those +2 bonus dies don't get a single success you get this infected Condition AND the paradox was made more severe.<br /> <br /> Then when you hit Baalim you are laughing to the bank because you're &quot;too dark to fail&quot;/too big to fail.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T01:51:48-07:00","id":1076370,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> Yea, it would be nice to have this sort of gambling, pushing the limits and overconfidence. Let's wait for SoS and see how it looks then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T02:29:28-07:00","id":1076377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076370#post1076370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7967\" data-vbnamecard=\"7967\">Scarlet Witch</a> Yea, it would be nice to have this sort of gambling, pushing the limits and overconfidence. Let's wait for SoS and see how it looks then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it going to be in SoS for sure? If so that is very exciting! I thought it wasn't, but I kind of assumed that... I don't know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:51:15-07:00","id":1076553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076370#post1076370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Yea, it would be nice to have this sort of gambling, pushing the limits and overconfidence. Let's wait for SoS and see how it looks then.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, there is nothing in the blogs or the forums that could indicate these new left-handed systems are going to be in SoS or in Tome of the Pentacle. Which is a damn shame, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:04:29-07:00","id":1076558,"title":"","content":"Yeah.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth the outline for the book was detailed <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, including the contents of each chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T10:10:56-07:00","id":1076562,"title":"","content":"I might have that wrong in this case. Wasn't it something that Dave said to publish in open development section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T01:38:39-07:00","id":1076853,"title":"","content":"It won't be in Sugns of Sorcery. we're trying to figure out a good place for them, even if it's just a web-issued mechanics update for Left Hand Path.<br /> <br /> I should reemphasise that unless you're a Nasnas, you can't use the Gnosis roll to control Paradox successes except on specially-made rotes or Praxes. In 1e, it only worked on rotes. Being able to improvise them is the mark of a second-initiation Scelestus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T01:45:39-07:00","id":1076856,"title":"","content":"Considering how good praxes are that's little consolation for the straight-and-narrow mages! Thanks Dave!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T02:48:51-07:00","id":1076872,"title":"","content":"So technically everyone didn't have the option to invite paradox into their spells? You have to be initiated first? Or am I missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11759-bonreu","name":"Bonreu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T02:56:35-07:00","id":1076876,"title":"","content":"You have to have a Befouled Praxis or rote, but you don't need any training to Befoul a Praxis when you buy it - just to know that it's possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T04:22:25-07:00","id":1076900,"title":"","content":"Have to say, I'm enjoying the description of this system a lot more than the one from 1E, where you could improvise-befoul any spell but it only translated to a reduction of the Paradox roll and resistant wounds complications. And the Joining either did or didn't let you throw Paradox on people, depending which of the two books you read that mentioned it.<br /> <br /> This whole 'gradual mastery of corruption' thing and the way it lets you supercharge spells is a lot more in-line with the Abyss as this force you let in, and balances better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come visit our unofficial Mage: the Awakening Discord Server!<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Z42DJ9h</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13241-biston","name":"Biston","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T04:27:29-07:00","id":1076902,"title":"","content":"Does it change the corebook thing about anyone being able to invite Paradox and roll Gnosis to control the outcome? We have an apostate self taught mage whose whole deal is that she figured it out on her own intuitively and was using it for years before meeting anyone from the magical society, and she definitely won't want (OOC and IC) to become a &quot;initiated&quot; Scelestus or buy extra rotes/praxes- the gray space of &quot;people look down at her and whisper she MIGHT be one because who knows&quot; was perfect for her.<br /> I guess the problem here was that she read the blurb about this in a way that separated Scelesti from other users of this &quot;trick&quot;; paraphrasing &quot;Any Mage can do it using this mechanic, and an actual Scelestus who bargains with the Abyss gains more control detailed by storyteller&quot;. Ugh, this is going to be a weird talk.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Ah, and to make it clear, I'm not bashing and bitching about the change. I welcome any change that forces Mages to &quot;specialize&quot; and narrow their focus so they have reasons to stick to certain spells and methods. I'm just in an awkward situation where this will change gameplay experience of one of our players *massively* and I know her well enough that I can safely assume she will not like the change, as it will just blarp all over the gameplay she enjoyed so far - which was interacting with Rotes, Praxes and other &quot;buy specific thing for a specific spell&quot; mechanics as less as possible in order to create a self taught mage who relies mostly on raw talent and improvised magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:16:02-07:00","id":1076926,"title":"","content":"I admit, I apparently misunderstood the whole Befouling thing. I thought it was something any Mage could do, and that was the power and temptation of it; that the Abyss was <i>right there</i>, and you didn't even need any special bargaining to use its power. It's a bit like a monkey finding out that there's a pile of hand grenades nearby; nothing <i>compels</i> it to do it, but... Hey...<br /> <br /> Requiring a rote or praxis for it might not mean much to NPCs, but, for players, that puts an XP cost in the way between them and it. The possibility of a Mage turning to using Befouled magic in a moment of panic and weakness disappears. I guess that might be for the best - there'd be way more Befouled spells, if that were the case - but it does remove the common angle from it.<br /> <br /> Still, can see why you'd go with that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:25:21-07:00","id":1076929,"title":"","content":"Mmmm. Well, I know that this will remain an NPC option forever in our circles now - people have an aversion to putting anything on their character sheet that might kill them (and &quot;kill Scelesti on sight&quot; is pretty much that) even if the chance of them being discovered is 1%. Kinda like how nobody ever would touch Dark Side Points in Star Wars Saga, because they were basically &quot;get enough of these and your character is an NPC&quot; or Taint in L5R*. Only thing that ever worked was temptation of &quot;just this once, with no permanent cost attached, crossed fingers&quot; bargain.<br /> The only exception is the guy who always went for &quot;tainted antagonist&quot; power options in oWoD, playing stuff like Nephandi/heavy diablerists/etc, but nobody wants to play with him because he is kind of a jerk and the power difference between his &quot;tainted&quot; characters and normal players was massive due to how efficient they often were, so he is haunting PBF games only now.<br /> <br /> I also realized that I really like the perspective of Joining 0 kicking you back into Wisdom, because it allows for redemption stories and gives me a leeway for &quot;maybe not every Scelesti is killed on sight&quot;. Hm.<br /> <br /> *Taint is, basically, a soul infection of evil that will slowly turn you into a monster. It has 5 stages, each 10 points long, and it's easy to stop at early stages. You can gain it by being in contaminated area, touching highly Tainted things, or using dark magics. There is no way to remove Taint Points thats accessible to players, and being Tainted basically removes you from public space and ability to have a social life, so getting to stage 1 is basically a &quot;retire your character&quot; sign. <br /> Which is a major problem for a GM...because Tainted creatures are kind of &quot;designated antagonists&quot; if you want to have some monster bashing. Because interacting with Taint can - and after enough rolls, it *will* - give you Taint, *players* avoid it as much as possible because one unlucky roll destroys their character. This leads into situations where Taint can't never be a real danger...because if it is, you literally can bring an end to your campaign right there and right now if something goes wrong. And you have no real control over it going wrong or not. <br /> <br /> The way I dealt with it was this: in basic rules, Taint can also be gained passively simply by having it inside you. You roll periodically to check if it got worse. If you succeeded, nothing happens; if you fail, you get more Taint. <br /> I added a caveat that characters can lose Taint, but never can go &quot;below&quot; their current Stage - so Stage 1 character can sit at 10 Taint points forever, but will never drop back to Stage 0, 9 Points. So until you get into Stage 1, you are just &quot;flirting with danger&quot;, so hitting your toe on a large tainted rock will not force you to retire your character.<br /> Setting wise, I allowed Stage 1 characters to still continue their normal lives, with a caveat of them being seen as suspicious and potentially dangerous by greater public and facing consequences coming from that; stuff like having to wear special marks that will identify you as a Tainted person to onlookers, and so on.<br /> This changed EVERYTHING, and people are finally not afraid to actually engage Tainted things, but still have to be careful enough to not overdo it. <br /> <br /> That's just something I wanted to share, because it came to my mind after Dave pondered upon if players would ever engage with Abyssal/&quot;evil&quot; mechanics earlier here. So in my experience - no if it's potentially permanently damning to their character without a way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:44:33-07:00","id":1076935,"title":"","content":"Oh, and on the other hand, I'm really curious if you will be able to play a Rabashakim &quot;player-character-party-friendly&quot;. If so, I'm really excited for a Adamantine Arrow who is a Rabashakim but still considers themselves to be a good pentacle person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T06:45:28-07:00","id":1076936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076853#post1076853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1e, it only worked on rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you're one of the authors of LHP but that's not right. It's states you can apply befouling to any spell, you just have to pass a resolve + composure roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:03:09-07:00","id":1076947,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I went back and double-checked that to find the addiction rules but I assumed I must have misread. It's there on page 65, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:28:21-07:00","id":1076958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076929#post1076929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just something I wanted to share, because it came to my mind after Dave pondered upon if players would ever engage with Abyssal/&quot;evil&quot; mechanics earlier here. So in my experience - no if it's potentially permanently damning to their character without a way out.</div> </div> </div> </div>My experience isn't quite the same. Back when my group played L5R, we've had quite a few characters getting Tainted, and we'd enjoy the drama that ensued: their pains keep it controlled for as long as needed to fulfill their duties, their embrace of a new power which they'd use for their personal/Clan's gain, their tragic ends when they lose control over it.<br /> Think it's a table expectations thing, as we all knew any of our characters could die at any moment, so we'd compete for the best &quot;closing scene&quot;, as it were.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:36:12-07:00","id":1076960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076958#post1076958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My experience isn't quite the same. Back when my group played L5R, we've had quite a few characters getting Tainted, and we'd enjoy the drama that ensued: their pains keep it controlled for as long as needed to fulfill their duties, their embrace of a new power which they'd use for their personal/Clan's gain, their tragic ends when they lose control over it.<br /> Think it's a table expectations thing, as we all knew any of our characters could die at any moment, so we'd compete for the best &quot;closing scene&quot;, as it were.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, except setting literally stated that if you are tainted, you have two choices: you commit suicide or accept a permanent house arrest while Witch Hunters periodically check your condition and will kill you when they decide it's bad enough or you start trying to have any kind of life.<br /> Well, you had the *third* choice of trying to hide it, but that would mean that you are going to get executed on sight if anyone gets a clue, and your immediate family will probably suffer traitor's brand at best or get purged at worst. And basically anyone barely honorable was conditioned into thinking that something like this is basically betraying the Empire and Celestial Order, so death is better than pretense of life.<br /> You could also end up in the barracks of Tainted Berserkers where, again, you would be expected to live in isolation until there is a need to throw some disposable troops in order to slowdown a marching megaoni or something.<br /> <br /> Either way, kiss your character and character concept goodbye, simply because you failed a Earth Ring roll to resist Taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T08:48:03-07:00","id":1076999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076960#post1076960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, except setting literally stated that if you are tainted, you have two choices: you commit suicide or accept a permanent house arrest while Witch Hunters periodically check your condition and will kill you when they decide it's bad enough or you start trying to have any kind of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>This on a setting which states it's highly dishonorable to fight duels to the death without permission from your superiors, <i>yet illegal duels happen all the time anyway</i>.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, you had the *third* choice of trying to hide it, but that would mean that you are going to get executed on sight if anyone gets a clue, and your immediate family will probably suffer traitor's brand at best or get purged at worst. And basically anyone barely honorable was conditioned into thinking that something like this is basically betraying the Empire and Celestial Order, so death is better than pretense of life. </div> </div> </div>Story fodder, right there.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Either way, kiss your character and character concept goodbye, simply because you failed a Earth Ring roll to resist Taint. </div> </div> </div>How's that any different from losing a character to a damage roll that happened to explode 3-4 times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:10:25-07:00","id":1077007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076902#post1076902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm just in an awkward situation where this will change gameplay experience of one of our players *massively* and I know her well enough that I can safely assume she will not like the change, as it will just blarp all over the gameplay she enjoyed so far .</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah. Why would you do that? Don't change it in a middle of the game if it might worsen her experience. It's unfair. Like that one childhood friend who was always finding new rules to fuck you up in a board game. Introduce it in the next chronicle or craft some merits for her.<br /> <br /> That said I don't see a reason for a player to use 'official' scelesti rules. It's just not worth it and you can't do it with improvised spells. No carrot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 04-12-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:05:36-07:00","id":1077045,"title":"","content":"Really? Clicking &quot;quote&quot; erases your whole post if you have written something before hitting it?! I'm so annoyed. I had a super large post about taint and illegal duelling and how &quot;instant death/character concepts deaths&quot; are contrary to genre of character-focused drama like CofD and L5R and it's all wasted now. I'm so, so so so so sad.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we will probably end up giving the player a custom merit to show that it's her awesome talent or something.<br /> <br /> My sadness is great. Anyway, being Tainted visibly mutates you and does a host of other things, and most importantly, turns you into an active danger to everyone in the Empire, surrendering your soul at the end to a vengeful God. Illegal dueling is one of these honorably illegal things that are &quot;better to act and ask for forgiveness later, than to wait for permission&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T13:33:52-07:00","id":1077177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1076876#post1076876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to have a Befouled Praxis or rote, but you don't need any training to Befoul a Praxis when you buy it - just to know that it's possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's an additional threshold (on top of knowing that it's even possible) that stops both players and characters from dabbling with Antinomian magic. Characters can't really be tempted to it in a weak or pressed moment since it requires an amount of effort to even learn how to do it, and I can see players skipping it because of the XP cost (even if they already plan on becoming Nasnasi since by then they wouldn't need befouled Praxes/Rotes anyway). I know it's just one XP to technically become a Rabashakim, but then you'd only have a single spell you're able to befoul. And I'd imagine you've already learned most spells you'd want to befoul as Praxes and Rotes already unless you're a very fresh mage.<br /> <br /> In case anyone else feels the same I can repeat the same suggestion I've already given to my group: Have it be possible for mages to befoul Praxes without having to learn new ones. I do actually like the concept of Antinomian Rotes as separate from regular Rotes since they're specialized Imagos, but Praxes are spells that a mage knows inside and out, and you could make an argument that you wouldn't have to relearn a spell you know by heart in order to befoul it as if it were a spell you were relatively unfamiliar with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:07:22-07:00","id":1077252,"title":"","content":"I also realized that it'd solve the problem of learning Antinomian Praxes. A regular Praxis is learned through dedicated practice or repetitive use of the spell. How the hell would you learn an Antinomian Praxis if you can't actually cast it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:12:04-07:00","id":1077259,"title":"","content":"I like an idea of &quot;specialized&quot; Praxes and Rotes, by the way. Basically, something that is bought just like a Praxis and a Rote, but can't be combined with normal Praxis or normal Rote. I feel that would be an interesting way to make them different, not necessarily stronger; &quot;forbidden magic&quot; being flat out better than &quot;straight magic&quot; always seemed like a problem to me. I prefer &quot;different in interesting, gameplay changing way&quot; than &quot;same ++&quot;.<br /> Imagine:<br /> <br /> Classic Praxis: Exceptional Threshold 3<br /> Befouled Praxis: Roll Gnosis to ride Paradox<br /> Classic Rote: Gain extra Reach<br /> Befouled Rote: Auto-Convert Paradox to Reach (example, no idea how Befouled Rote should look like)<br /> + these options being mutually exclusive in a single casting. Gives you a reason to stick to the classics, but still allows you to have a reason to pick Befouled options; also, opens up a design space that doesn't &quot;bloat&quot; options that can apply to a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:44:51-07:00","id":1077293,"title":"","content":"For when you don't want to spend the XP on buying a befouled Rote, keep every Scelesti Grimoire you &quot;stumble&quot; across. It won't be protected by Sanctity of Merits unless you buy it as a Merit later, but hey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:49:26-07:00","id":1077298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077252#post1077252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also realized that it'd solve the problem of learning Antinomian Praxes. A regular Praxis is learned through dedicated practice or repetitive use of the spell. How the hell would you learn an Antinomian Praxis if you can't actually cast it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that once you know it's possible you have to cast the spell repeatedly -trying- to befoul the spell, which probably involves adding a lot of Reach. Eventually, you've cast it as many times as necessary to internalize it as a Praxis and the befouling part of drawing on Abyssal energy to mesh with the spell is internalized along with it, the greater level of intimacy with the spell fuses with your familiarity of forcing the Abyss to interact with it and it becomes officially befouled.<br /> <br /> So basically, knowledge, lots of failed dry runs, eventual internalization into Praxis, finally success at befouling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:01:19-07:00","id":1077309,"title":"","content":"Maybe there is some interesting learning mechanic for them. Who knows if you pay it in XP? Maybe you pay by decreasing your Wisdom willingly when your spell provokes a Paradox related Act of Hubris, or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T17:21:04-07:00","id":1077348,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of using a merit. In the game I'm currently in (it is just a 1-on-1 game), my character has a merit that makes all her spells antinomian if she is using the merit at the time, but it also forces all the spells to be antinomian... it also tainted her blood and made her need to bleed herself to near death within 3 hours or she suffers an aneurysm and dies. And with the existence of cool merits like &quot;summoner's soul&quot;, there's no reason to make a fuss unless the other players start moaning about not updating to the new rules.<br /> <br /> edit: I am seriously considering trying to make a homebrew for scelesti magic since dave's hands are tied with deviant. I was kind of thinking something that works like its own spellfactor list, like scale and duration, but instead, it is for abyssal magic.<br /> <br /> You can already spend reach on things like advanced potency or sensory range, so an abyssal equivalent might be spending paradox reach from your gnosis roll on such effects from Left-Hand Path, and ontop, you could accept +paradox dice for +gnosis on the control roll, for hideous gambling potential, but it would probably be limited by your Joining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","user":"Scarlet Witch","date":". 04-12-2017, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T02:51:11-07:00","id":1077597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077045#post1077045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Clicking &quot;quote&quot; erases your whole post if you have written something before hitting it?! I'm so annoyed. I had a super large post about taint and illegal duelling and how &quot;instant death/character concepts deaths&quot; are contrary to genre of character-focused drama like CofD and L5R and it's all wasted now. I'm so, so so so so sad.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we will probably end up giving the player a custom merit to show that it's her awesome talent or something.<br /> <br /> My sadness is great. Anyway, being Tainted visibly mutates you and does a host of other things, and most importantly, turns you into an active danger to everyone in the Empire, surrendering your soul at the end to a vengeful God. Illegal dueling is one of these honorably illegal things that are &quot;better to act and ask for forgiveness later, than to wait for permission&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that sucks. Was legitimately interested in reading your thoughts on that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is: Taint worked perfectly at my table, for the stories we wanted to tell, because we fully expected handling spiritual toxic waste would only have negative consequences in the long run. Admittedly, my table might be an outlier, but it was never an issue.<br /> <br /> I do agree with you on the point that this wouldn't fly in Mage, but for a different reason: I'm expecting the Abyss to be <i>tempting</i>. You can become Tainted against your will, but nobody's going to force to infuse your spells with Paradox. For Antinomian magic to work in the role I'm expecting it to fill, there needs to be a just-this-time clause, a way for characters to feel like &quot;I know what I did was bad, but it was the best option I had at the time&quot;, a way to make them think &quot;I can deal with the consequences, sure&quot;.<br /> (I hope this last bit was coherent, coffee machine broke down)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:26:01-07:00","id":1077847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075056#post1075056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's homebrew.<br /> <br /> We haven't had time yet to 2e the Scelesti mechanics beyond the one-line description of first initiation everyone's talking about. You can, if you know how to, attempt to control how a Paradox manifests, but the process is extremely addictive and runs the risk of you becoming a second-stage Scelesti (a Nasnasi), where your Path symbols are corrupted by their abyssal antitheses, your ability to summon supernal creatures is replaced by one to summon Gulmoth, and your nimbus is poisioned.<br /> <br /> Third initiation Scelesti are just those with Legacies, some of which require you to be a Nasnas.<br /> <br /> Fourth Initiation Scelesti are those who bargain with the Aeon of Paradox for the ability to mess with the Paradox roll, not just how any Paradox appears. Their powers require the most work.<br /> <br /> The thing that we're noodling about, playtesting when Scelesti come up in our games, is to replace Wisdom for Nasnasi-and-up Scelesti to represent their fucked-up natures. Scelesti probably become Qliphoth instead of Mad Ones when they completely go off the edge.<br /> <br /> Oh, right, yeah. A Qliphoth is a mage who is a walking Iris to a Annunaki, spawning Gulmoth wherever they go. They're in the &quot;way too powerful for even most mages to do anything other than run&quot; category along with Exarchal avatars and archmasters.<br /> <br /> Yeah, so my version currently calls it &quot;Joining&quot; after the original name for the second initiation from back in Tome of Mysteries; it goes up where Wisdom goes down. 0 Joining you turn back into a normal Mage with Wisdom 1 (it was always canonical that nasnasi could, in theory, go cold turkey and return to normalcy), 10 Joining turns you into a Qliphoth, the trick to being a Scelestus is to fuck your Path's symbolism just enough but not too much; to draw on your linked Annunaki without being consumed by it. The experiments are in what causes it to go up and down; what's a &quot;sin&quot; for a Scelestus?<br /> <br /> It's a parallel to Tremere, who in the protoype 2e notes replace their Gnosis with &quot;Hollow&quot;, the trait that lets their Gnosis consume the soul currently attached to it as fuel, gives them Houses instead of Legacies, and so on. The Tremere are the most complex fallen mages because they're both an altered template , a group of not-exactly-Legacies and an Order, and it's figuring out what parts of them are inherent powers, what's the various Legacies they've consumed being turned into Houses, and what's the Tremere-Order-Status-only Merit equivalents to Egregore, etc that's the trick. But Tremere *do* use Wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is most interesting and exciting, and I do so hope a properly developed version of this material gets published sooner rather than later, optimally in some supplement that can get the PoD treatment, but in a pinch even a PDF update of LHP would do. This revision makes me wonder, in 1ed Qliphoth were the sad fate of an Archmage that really screwed up Imperial magic, and so fairly rare. By these new rules it seems any 'ordinary' Nasnasi-and-up mage that overindulges in use of Abyssal magic and fills up their Joining meter can become one, so they ought to be rather more frequent than before. Yet they are told to be too powerful for most mages to deal with. So what polices Qliphoth and stops them from screwing up the Tellurian at large? Archmages and Supernal Ochemata? By the way, 1e rules told a Scelestus mage that tries to make a deal with the Old Man to gain the Elder Diamond would become a living incarnation of the Abyss if they really screw up their pacts. Are these, too, Qliphoth by another name?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:36:51-07:00","id":1077852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075124#post1075124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reactions also vary by Order - a Silver Ladder mage who casts a Befouled rote once to achieve a set goal and never touches it again is a badass if he gets caught, a Guardian of the Veil who does it will be lucky to walk away with intact frontal lobes.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason the Orders dress Befouling up in Babylonian terminology and make Rabashakim out to be different, somehow, is that they don't want neophyte mages knowing how <i>easy</i> it is.<br /> <br /> But just as abstinance is the worst sex education policy, making abyssal magic more Mysterious than it is just means those who find put about it and experiment with it do so without a safety net AND go hardcore quicker. you get way fewer Rabashakim, but more of them blow up into Nasnasi.<br /> <br /> Again with the Tremere side-commentary, but the major fallout of the Tremere's banishment is that well-meaning Legacies who have extreme longevity or immortality among their practices have to hush it up in polite company, and the modern Pentacle knows way less about Souls and how they work than their ancestors from a few thousand years ago, because Souls were the Tremere's &quot;thing&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>How saddening and infuriating even the most enlightened and mentally/spiritually advanced supernatural offshoot of mankind has not yet learned the lesson in millennia about the pettiness, stupidity, and (self-)destructive nature of demonization of knowledge, guilt by association, and moral panic. Especially given the utter, overwhelming futility of pursuing willful ignorance for a supernatural splat whose defining psych trait is obsessive curiosity. Then again, their mundane cousins have not yet really learnt the equally poignant and inescapable lesson in millennia that prohibition of pleasurable stimuli never ever works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T12:42:35-07:00","id":1077856,"title":"","content":"I'm confused. If according to the new rules a Rabashkim can only use Befouled praxes and rotes, and it takes progression to Nasnasus to use Befouled improvised magic, how self-taught dabblers in Abyssal magic w/o contact with other Scelesti (which are supposed to be far from rare) are supposed to become both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:02:38-07:00","id":1077909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077852#post1077852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How saddening and infuriating even the most enlightened and mentally/spiritually advanced supernatural offshoot of mankind has not yet learned the lesson in millennia about the pettiness, stupidity, and (self-)destructive nature of demonization of knowledge, guilt by association, and moral panic. Especially given the utter, overwhelming futility of pursuing willful ignorance for a supernatural splat whose defining psych trait is obsessive curiosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's clearly not futile; it does work to a degree. The Abstinence education analogy isn't 1 to 1 as teenagers still generally have some idea what sex is. Befouling is an idea you really have to learn or work out yourself, it's not easily intuited.<br /> <br /> Also teenagers having sex generally doesn't cause the walls of reality to crumble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:04:10-07:00","id":1077911,"title":"","content":"Unless it's a horror movie. Or, even worse, a slasher movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T14:59:03-07:00","id":1077948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077856#post1077856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused. If according to the new rules a Rabashkim can only use Befouled praxes and rotes, and it takes progression to Nasnasus to use Befouled improvised magic, how self-taught dabblers in Abyssal magic w/o contact with other Scelesti (which are supposed to be far from rare) are supposed to become both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages know how to run experiments and are driven to Obsession in their pursuits and they can experience the Abyss as an observable phenomenon and interact with its denizens so this is a relatively small hurdle to overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:13:58-07:00","id":1077960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077856#post1077856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused. If according to the new rules a Rabashkim can only use Befouled praxes and rotes, and it takes progression to Nasnasus to use Befouled improvised magic, how self-taught dabblers in Abyssal magic w/o contact with other Scelesti (which are supposed to be far from rare) are supposed to become both?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you use the Befouled praxis one too many times until you have an abyssal awakening at a ziggurat? In 1E there was a count-down to when your overuse of antinomian magic in a short time-frame would result in the Joining, with or without direction. The countdown was decided by your willpower dots. Each time you used a befouled spell, you got an increasing penalty to resist the temptation to cast your next spell as antinomian as well--if the penalty reduced your dice pool to a chance die, you immediately became nasnasi, even without a teacher. You then gained the abyssal insight needed to expand your powers--or you could turn your back on the abyss, a painful process, and free yourself--but it would also make you unable to ever again use antinomian magic at all.<br /> Dunno if that helps explain it, but if you need to homebrew temporarily, maybe that's a good start? as mrmdubois said, Obsession can get you places :3<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:23:48-07:00","id":1077970,"title":"","content":"All in all, the 2e mechanics mean that Befouling is now more like premediated murder than involuntary manslaughter, in the sense that you had to actively seek the Abyss out and make an effort to bring it into this world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T15:50:25-07:00","id":1077981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077909#post1077909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it's clearly not futile; it does work to a degree. The Abstinence education analogy isn't 1 to 1 as teenagers still generally have some idea what sex is. Befouling is an idea you really have to learn or work out yourself, it's not easily intuited.<br /> <br /> Also teenagers having sex generally doesn't cause the walls of reality to crumble.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just about Befouling. There is also the fact the Pentacle has demonized valuable knowledge about the nature of souls and life-extension magic out of moral panic about the Tremere, who for all their nastiness aren't going to cause the walls of reality to crumble, or do much worse than any mundane serial killer, in the foreseeable future. Guilt by association is just stupid and harmful. Moreover, Scelesti in all evidence have been thriving in the last few millennia, so I've my doubts suppressing knowledge about the Abyss is that effective a strategy to combat them. As Dave said, in the end you trade less dabblers for more dedicated cultists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-13-2017, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T17:57:59-07:00","id":1078053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077852#post1077852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How saddening and infuriating even the most enlightened and mentally/spiritually advanced supernatural offshoot of mankind has not yet learned the lesson in millennia about the pettiness, stupidity, and (self-)destructive nature of demonization of knowledge, guilt by association, and moral panic. Especially given the utter, overwhelming futility of pursuing willful ignorance for a supernatural splat whose defining psych trait is obsessive curiosity. Then again, their mundane cousins have not yet really learnt the equally poignant and inescapable lesson in millennia that prohibition of pleasurable stimuli never ever works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading Dave's post again, I think what what happened here is not a systematic demonization of knowledge, but the logical consequence of booting out the only experts in the field.<br /> <br /> When talking about Befouling, we're talking about the magical equivalent of human experiments done by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unit_731\" target=\"_blank\">Unit 731</a> here. Just... look at the link. The knowledge that such horrible things <i>can </i>and <i>have been </i>done, and just what horrors they unleashed, is enough. Do we really want details on <i>how </i>they did it? For what?<br /> <br /> And besides, for soul-working and immortality stuff, it's been already looked at askance well before the Tremere. Like how early Guardians were suspected as Banishers, Tremere were most likely suspected as Reapers/Liches. But as where the Guardians of the Veil cooperated with Awakened society, the Tremere crossed the line by assimilating Reaper Legacies instead of merely studying them, and even turned their Gnosis into something else. This in turn 'confirmed' the suspicions against the Tremere, and that led to the banishment. It just happened so that because the Diamond worked on division of labor/expertise, so when a whole wing fell there was no one to replace them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:08:38-07:00","id":1078163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1077981#post1077981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the fact the Pentacle has demonized valuable knowledge about the nature of souls and life-extension magic out of moral panic about the Tremere, who for all their nastiness aren't going to cause the walls of reality to crumble, or do much worse than any mundane serial killer, in the foreseeable future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a guarantee. The Tremere's mythology believes in a sixth watchtower, deep in the Abyss. It's entirely possible it's just another Abyssal incursion waiting for the Tremere to bring it into the Fallen World and cause reality to crumble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guilt by association is just stupid and harmful. Moreover, Scelesti in all evidence have been thriving in the last few millennia, so I've my doubts suppressing knowledge about the Abyss is that effective a strategy to combat them. As Dave said, in the end you trade less dabblers for more dedicated cultists. </div> </div> </div>Mages are human. They're group oriented and see threats in people who don't side with them. Seeing anything good in the Abyss flies in the face of most of the Diamond Orders beliefs and history. Plus I have to imagine there's more than a little Exarchic influence. The rulers of the world don't want it glitching out of their control and the Abyss seems like the only real threat to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:44:27-07:00","id":1078171,"title":"","content":"Me, I'd be happy if we finally have rules for interacting with Qlippoth, even if it is &quot;here's a list of things you do to escape the inside of one, and rules for making your own challenges.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T22:03:39-07:00","id":1078177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1078171#post1078171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me, I'd be happy if we finally have rules for interacting with Qlippoth, even if it is &quot;here's a list of things you do to escape the inside of one, and rules for making your own challenges.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think every line could seriously use some in-depth storytellers advice. A lot is being left in the hands of the storytellers to develop, but not everyone comes to the game with a good understanding of developing mechanics for them. I haven't thoroughly looked through the Demon's Storyteller Guide, perhaps that has something for them. And it does look like Signs of Sorcery will at least broaden our idea of what Supernal magic is capable of. Acrozatarim's Giver of Gifts posts were great for seeing how Gifts should be developed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2017, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T02:30:46-07:00","id":1078233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1078171#post1078171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Me, I'd be happy if we finally have rules for interacting with Qlippoth, even if it is &quot;here's a list of things you do to escape the inside of one, and rules for making your own challenges.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>For starters, aren't Qliphoth things that absorb you into their worlds but also not <i>literally?</i> I got the impression from all the bits about them in 1E that from the absorbed's perspective, they're in a different place, but outsiders will be able to find the absorbed person wandering the fallen material world in a fit of madness, similar to the Qliphoth itself. Right? Or is the absorption literal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T04:51:25-07:00","id":1078273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1078233#post1078233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For starters, aren't Qliphoth things that absorb you into their worlds but also not <i>literally?</i> I got the impression from all the bits about them in 1E that from the absorbed's perspective, they're in a different place, but outsiders will be able to find the absorbed person wandering the fallen material world in a fit of madness, similar to the Qliphoth itself. Right? Or is the absorption literal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get that too, but that doesn't mean you're not also still inside of one. Your body may be outside, but your mind is in the corrupted Golden Road, and in Mage, being inside of the Astral Plane makes where your body is a bit of a technical issue. And what is <i>definitely </i>inside of them are a whole gaggle of acamoth, as a side effect of them being avatars of the Annunaki-what's the odds on them <i>not</i> having ways to strike at the physical body through the perspective, 666 to 1? Per acamoth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T21:04:00-07:00","id":1096591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074886-controlling-paradox-scelesti?p=1075097#post1075097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, the wordcount pressures and priorities for the corebook were such that we made the hard call - we couldmonly provide playable rules for one of the Pentacle's enemies, and in service to The Fallen World Chronicle (and efficiency, as they have the least special rules) we went for the Seers. If you're a storyteller, you don't *need* any of the rules for Joining we're working on - just to know that a Nasnasi can roll Gnosis and control how Paradox Reach is spent on released paradoxes. I guess the full rules with conditions for creating a Befouled Praxis or learning a Befouled rote (and therefore being a rabashakim) will be interesting for troupes wanting their pcs to play with fire, but part of me does wonder how many people would actually <i>use</i> systems for being a Baal.<br /> <br /> Tremere, though, are an Order. A secretive, hated-by-the-others Order who were expelled from the Diamond in the middle ages for eating souls, but they're the point where the venn diagram bubbles of &quot;Nameless Order&quot;, &quot;Legacy,&quot; &quot;Reaper&quot; and &quot;Lich&quot; all meet. If they were Abyssal, too, they'd be all the Mage bad guys combined!</div> </div> </div> </div>I virtually guarantee I would try it as a player at least once just like the Tremere and definitely would like the rules as a GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}